spec se04-self-conflict-through-frontier: 2 sessions, 2 permutations
# SE04. s0 holds its commit instant (the commit hold). s1 sets t.v = 1 through a cypher.Session and the
# commit acknowledges. s1 then rewrites its own node twice: SESSIONLESS (t.v = 2), whose
# snapshot is the held frontier, below s1's own commit, so it finds s1's version
# committed after its snapshot and is refused (first-updater-wins, F2); and through
# its SESSION (t.v = 3), which waits in the background for its own commit and, once
# s0 publishes, is not refused. The control interleaving publishes s0 first: both
# rewrites succeed.

starting permutation: s0w s0a s1w s1sl s1aw s1wait s0p s1rel
step s0w: lpg: SetNodeProperty(s, v, 1)
step s0a: lpg: Graph.AllocateCommitTS (instant reserved, not published)
step s1w: <cypher.Session, deadline 30s> MATCH (n:T {name:'t'}) SET n.v = 1 RETURN n.v AS v
v
-
1
(1 row)
step s1sl: <sessionless> MATCH (n:T {name:'t'}) SET n.v = 2 RETURN n.v AS v
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s1aw: <start cypher.Session in the background> MATCH (n:T {name:'t'}) SET n.v = 3 RETURN n.v AS v
